    "suggested_fix": "Do not apply the sentence-start exemption when a reading of the run spells a listed TLD and the run is not an ordinary capitalised English word (e.g. only exempt runs whose as-is lower form is a dictionary word such as 'it', 'in', 'is', 'if', or the word 'I'), or when the preceding token is a name joined by a dot/separator. Add regressions for '. ', ': ', '! ', '? ' separators with Iy/Iive/Iink/Ioan.",
